WEBVTT

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:09.980
Stand strong!

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.990
Not even these demons are immortal!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.300
But...

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.030
There are so many of them!

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.280
I won't be killed by the likes of you!

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.180
The soldiers are being pushed back!

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.460
We need to support them!

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.210
But we're surrounded!

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.550
Are you safe, Gilles?

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.300
Oh, Jeanne!

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.960
Beloved children of God,

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.760
Orléans is right in front of our eyes!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.260
Now is the time to charge 
forward with all our might!

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.290
For France, our homeland!

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.940
Follow me!

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.830
That's right! We have...

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.730
The Holy Maiden!

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.030
So that's Jeanne d'Arc...

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.670
Our homeland of France is embroiled
in an endless war with England.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.800
The English army comes to surround Orléans,

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.680
a strategically significant city
 in the heart of France.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.390
But then the French army arrives, 
led by a single young girl

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.650
who drives off the English.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.790
That girl is Jeanne d'Arc,

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:58.030
who would later become known 
as the Maid of Orléans.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.030
The Maid of Orléans

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:05.320
But it wasn't the English 
who surrounded Orléans this time.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.870
No, it was the monsters you called villains.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.690
And that's why we joined the battle.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.140
The Story Zone of Jeanne d'Arc...

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.360
Since she's the main character, 
she's really popular.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:24.390
So far, everything seems to be
 following their Books of Fate,

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.360
other than the English becoming villains.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.410
But we don't know how that's 
going to change from here out.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.270
We need to find the Chaos Teller
 as soon as possible.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.710
Today, we took back our home from the demons!

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:44.910
What greater proof could there 
be that God is on our side?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.760
So, what do we do now?

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.090
Gather information, I think.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.660
We need to find a lead on the Chaos Teller.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.440
What's up, kid?

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.210
Oh...

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.760
She's not that much older 
than we are, is she?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.840
Yet she's standing so tall...

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.760
What? You in love?

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:10.470
Did you already forget about Cinderella?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.390
O-Of course not!

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.770
That's...

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.290
What is it?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.700
Over there...

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:22.630
Sorry.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.240
I was probably imagining things.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:31.550
Meung-sur-Loire will be a focal 
point for the battles to come.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.360
As soon as our forces are ready, 
we'll take it back.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.460
Understood.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.310
But we're not fighting the English. 
We're fighting those monsters.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:43.760
My Book of Fate says we'll be
 victorious in our next battle, but...

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.890
It matters not who our opponent is.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.970
I will march towards victory regardless.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.740
What will you do, my guests?

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.220
I'm terribly sorry.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:57.150
We may have stepped in during 
the siege of Orléans, but...

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:01.830
It wouldn't be right for us to 
help one country over the other.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:03.320
Yeah.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.730
You needn't force yourselves.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:09.410
I'm simply grateful you decided 
to lend us your aid today.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.550
Without it, victory would have
 been out of reach.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.410
You have my sincere thanks.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.420
Excuse me.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:20.840
The citizens are asking 
to see Jeanne the Holy Maiden.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.070
Very well.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.990
If that will put their hearts at ease...

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.940
Is that all right, Gilles?

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.740
Yes.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.950
We can finalize our strategy later.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.810
I'm going to go watch.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.900
There'll be trouble if any villains survived.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:43.970
What's wrong, missy?

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.880
Don't tell me you're jealous.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.950
Of course not.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.230
But...

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.120
But?

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.120
I hope he doesn't get too involved again.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.790
Um... Might I have a word?

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.730
What is it, Ex?

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:04.170
Does your Book of Fate say 
you'll lead France to victory?

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.010
Why do you ask?

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:11.390
It's just that... You seemed so confident.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.790
No matter what end awaits me,

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:20.520
I will march forward for 
the sake of my homeland.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.990
That kid was incredible.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.410
Yeah. She was so tiny,
 but she ate like a troop of ten men.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:44.630
You!

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.510
Oh, hello there.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.760
So it <i>was</i> you I saw!

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.260
Here. Come sit with me.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.390
This stale bread is delicious.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.020
If you're here, then is the Chaos Teller
 of this Story Zone here, too?

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.520
Why are you so concerned 
with Jeanne d'Arc's fate?

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.900
Why...?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.820
You don't seem to know how her story ends.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:16.290
She'll be executed by the British in Rouen.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.970
Her homeland, France, will abandon her.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:24.770
As long as she's Jeanne d'Arc, 
there will be no escaping that fate.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:25.710
You're lying!

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.210
I'm telling the truth.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:30.400
I may be blind,

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:34.640
but my eyes can see glimpses of the 
flow of fate in each Story Zone.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.000
You're angry over her fate, aren't you?

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:43.350
Then, Ex, let me ask you...

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.340
What do you want to protect more?

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:50.240
Her life? Or her fate?

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.800
I...

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.570
I just...

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.490
Curly?

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:04.630
That Jeanne girl sure was amazing.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:08.750
Yeah. Maybe she really can 
hear the voice of God...

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:09.730
What happened?!

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:18.800
Man, what a feast.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.640
Boss didn't eat as much as usual.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.480
What happened with Aladdin 
must still be bothering her.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:29.030
And the new kid's obsessed with Jeanne...

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:30.860
I don't know what to do.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:33.650
I think I understand how the kid feels.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:39.480
I remember what it was like to be in awe
 of an amazing main character.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:42.120
That's just how men are, you see.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.880
I'm afraid I don't get it at all.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:49.580
Hey now, don't be like that.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.900
You feel the same way about guns...

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:56.550
What was that?

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:04.790
Um...

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.400
Ex? What is it?

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.410
I heard something that's been bothering me...

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.690
Bothering you?

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:14.970
Yes.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.530
About your fate.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:24.040
I am to be burned at the stake 
after being declared a heretic.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.360
That's terrible!

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.420
Aren't you scared?

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:31.850
What scares me the most isn't death.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:33.870
It's failing to achieve what I believe in.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:34.970
What you believe in?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:38.800
A world where my homeland is united 
and everyone can live in peace.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.590
I was born to make that happen.

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:43.100
That's why I'm alive now.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.710
But even if I die...

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:51.770
My feelings will be passed on, take human 
form, and someday change the world.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:55.230
Only when there's no one for those 
feelings to be passed on to

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:59.320
will the soul of Jeanne d'Arc 
 truly be destroyed.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:03.240
Then I will destroy your soul here and now!

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:06.540
You're...

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:11.040
Feel the hatred of England!

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:12.710
Watch out!

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.210
Ex!

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.820
You should've stayed out of this...

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:25.270
But no matter. Anyone who 
works with the French is an enemy!

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:26.770
Take this!

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.600
Cursed maiden...

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:39.820
Your execution at Meung-sur-Loire 
will be a glorious one!

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.860
The flames shall reach the heavens themselves!

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:45.320
W-Wait!

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:50.330
Are you okay?!

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:51.750
Were we too late?!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:55.040
Hold still. I'll use my healing magic...

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.560
Forget about me... Jeanne is...

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:04.970
The Chaos Teller is going to execute 
Jeanne at Meung-sur-Loire...

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.980
Ex!

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:24.870
General Gilles left before dawn, it looks like.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:28.790
Yeah. We need to follow him.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.250
Is the new kid going to be okay?

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:34.150
It should be safer here.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:39.310
And if we defeat the Chaos Teller, 
the curse on Ex should be broken.

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:42.700
Either way, we should get going.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.550
Okay! We're down a member,

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.060
but the Tao family is rolling out!

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.650
Everyone left to save 
Jeanne d'Arc, didn't they?

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.250
You...

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:05.590
I came because I had a 
question I wanted to ask you.

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:06.790
Ask me?

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.410
Your wild crest is a special power 
that lets you connect to any hero.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.380
It's a sign of your infinite potential.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.550
How do you intend to use it?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.480
Nothing you do will ever mean anything.

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.020
Unlike those of us with blank books,

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:32.850
normal folk can never escape the fates 
laid out for them by the Storyteller.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.740
So you are...

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:40.590
The Church of Fortem is composed entirely 
of people who hold blank books.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.360
We wish to free the people
 from the Storyteller.

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:46.160
The Church of Fortem...

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:51.500
I know you've seen many 
terrible fates in your journeys.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:59.290
So if you also wish to save those poor 
people from their cruel fates...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.300
Won't you join us?

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:09.390
We're almost to Meung-sur-Loire.

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:14.080
It's been a long, long time since 
it was just the three of us.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.470
How long has it been since the new kid joined?

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:21.070
I can't say exactly, but it's been some time now.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.660
He doesn't stand out too much when he is here,

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.760
but I feel like something's
 missing when he's not.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:27.880
Yeah.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:30.410
At some point, it just became 
natural to have him here.

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:33.870
He's still got a lot to learn, though.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:37.370
He loves sticking his nose in things.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.280
Yeah.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:41.640
I guess you could say he's too kind, 
in both a good and a bad way.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.750
He gets a little too involved 
in other people's fates.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:49.140
We're just travelers passing through.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.710
But there's nothing we can do.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:57.060
It's Ex's decision to make.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:02.440
Well, from his perspective, 
we may be a little cold.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:06.150
If we do defeat the Chaos Teller 
and remove the curse...

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:10.570
Do you think he'll keep traveling with us?

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:14.430
That's something else
 we can't do anything about.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:15.860
You know?

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:17.650
Yeah.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:24.880
Join you?

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.580
Where are you going?

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.610
I have to follow Reina and the others.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.940
If I don't hurry, Jeanne will...

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:40.440
Why do you follow such a meaningless path?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.900
Jeanne's fate has already been decided.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:46.400
That's... That's not the point.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:50.360
It doesn't matter if it means anything or not.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.440
Even if Jeanne is fated to be executed,

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.000
now's not the time for that!

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:01.370
Then you'll fight for fate?

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.960
It's not for fate.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.830
It's Jeanne's feelings...

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.550
Yes, that's what I truly want to protect!

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:16.680
Because they're her feelings, 
and nobody else's!

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.530
Cinderella's feelings...

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:27.490
Don Quixote's feelings...

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:30.700
All their feelings...

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:33.490
You're hopeless.

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:38.080
What are you doing?

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.220
I broke the curse.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:42.050
You should be fine now.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:54.010
I have other questions, but for now...

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:55.990
Thank you.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.270
So in the end, that's the 
fate you choose, isn't it?

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.760
It's too far to see.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.360
I guess we'll have to get a bit closer.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.870
General Gilles!

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:18.740
You came?

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:21.870
We were ambushed by the demons.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.920
My unit was wiped out.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:25.240
Wiped out?

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:28.590
So they knew you'd come 
to take back the city?

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:32.190
The execution will be held soon.

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.090
Please, save Jeanne!

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:40.850
Fools!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.270
The bastard keeps appearing and disappearing!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:54.780
I was born from the rage and 
hatred of the people of England!

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:58.030
I have no physical body!

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:01.510
Very well! Then I will use my deadly arrows!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.420
What's wrong?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.790
Aren't you going to shoot?

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.610
He's a cheater...

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:12.710
Even rabbits get mad sometimes!

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:24.480
You...

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:32.320
I'll execute you all before Jeanne!

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:33.700
Damn it...

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:35.530
This is bad.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:37.530
Are you ready?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.320
Yup.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.570
Hey, missy!

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:44.530
Are you ready to accept the baptism of death?

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:45.430
Reina!

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:51.590
I saved Jeanne!

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.490
Look who it is!

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:54.550
Nice work!

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.250
Ex...

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.930
Hang on. I'll take him out now.

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:02.410
You...

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:04.890
How can you move under my curse?

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:08.790
I was worried sick about you!

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:10.480
You're such a jerk!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:13.200
Sorry for worrying you, Reina.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.320
But I'm back.

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:16.650
Welcome back, Ex.

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:21.830
What can one more of you do?

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.100
If you're curious, we'll show you.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:26.270
It's time for the Tao family's counterattack!

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.580
Pay attention!

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:30.130
Alice!

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:31.580
Kai!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.550
Goliath!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.630
Gerda!

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:36.670
Connect!

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:52.500
Is it time for another adventure
 in Wonderland?

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.900
Filthy heretics...

00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:58.860
Here we go!

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.200
It won't work!

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:06.450
Frozen World!

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:10.210
Blizzard Heart!

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:13.890
Again?

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:14.630
He disappeared?

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.130
Are you willing to let Jeanne die, too?

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:25.010
I knew you'd do that!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.560
I'll show you what a true lady can do!

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.110
Wonder Labyrinth!

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.700
My body feels so light...

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.460
It seems like the curse has been lifted.

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.450
Good...

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.670
I knew you'd come save me.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:56.260
Feelings are passed on to others,

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:58.250
and become a power that can change the world.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:02.600
I can't even understand half 
of what that means, but...

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.280
When I heard you say that,

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.090
I remembered what an old knight once told me.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:13.020
He said that regardless of his fate, 
he would never betray what he believed in.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.190
What happened to him after that?

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:20.400
He stayed true to his beliefs 
until the very end.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.200
I see.

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:26.110
We're about to restore this world
 to the way it should be.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:28.780
I'm afraid this is goodbye.

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:29.910
Ex...

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.540
I have one last wish.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:38.250
Please take the feelings I bear 
along with you on your journey.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.060
I understand.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:43.390
No matter what fate you meet,

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:45.970
know that what you believed in was right.

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:48.350
Thank you.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.060
I'll begin, then.

00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:00.990
Teller of tales, 
drowned in a maelstrom of chaos...

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:05.070
By my words, I now begin the tuning...

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:24.200
Beloved children of God, 
Orléans is right in front of us!

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:27.340
Follow me, for France!

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.910
Now everything's back to how it was.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:33.980
Yeah.

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:40.480
<i>She'll be executed by the British in Rouen.</i>

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.980
<i>Her homeland, France, will abandon her.</i>

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:45.750
Why the long face, kid?

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:49.800
There's no room for gloom in the Tao family!

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:50.620
Yeah...

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:52.960
Oh, come on.

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:56.000
Aren't you supposed to be
 carrying her feelings?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:21:59.170
You're right.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:01.380
Let's go, everyone.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:04.960
Jeez, you sure are a handful, new kid.

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:07.960
You certainly are.

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:14.470
Beware the Jabberwock!

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:18.980
The jaws that bite, the claws that catch!

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:22.980
Beware the Jubjub bird...

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:29.310
The Jabberwock, with eyes of flame,

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.360
came whiffling through the tulgey wood,

00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:35.530
and burbled as it came!
